<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Battle of Cancha Rayada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1818</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chilean-war-of-independence">Chilean War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Battle of Cancha Rayada was fought on the night of 19 March 1818 near Talca, when royalist forces under Mariano Osorio surprised the camp of the patriot army of San Martín and O'Higgins and scattered it. O'Higgins was wounded, but the patriots regrouped and destroyed the royalist army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maipu">Battle of Maipú</a> two weeks later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-battle-of-cancha-rayada.jpg" alt="Second Battle of Cancha Rayada" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: B1mbo · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_loc_Maule.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
